{
  "name": "Strategy Blog Publisher",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "cronExpression",
              "expression": "0 12 * * 0"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "a1b2c3d4-0001-0001-0001-000000000001",
      "name": "Every Sunday 12pm",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [180, 300],
      "notes": "Runs after the blog compiler (10am) and tweet thread writer (11am) have both finished."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "command": "cd /Users/prashantchandel/Documents/strategy-blog && python3 publish.py 2>&1; echo \"EXIT:$?\""
      },
      "id": "a1b2c3d4-0002-0002-0002-000000000002",
      "name": "Run Publisher",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.executeCommand",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [420, 300],
      "notes": "Runs publish.py which posts the blog to the website and the tweet thread to Twitter."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "string": [
            {
              "value1": "={{ $json.stdout }}",
              "operation": "contains",
              "value2": "EXIT:0"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "a1b2c3d4-0003-0003-0003-000000000003",
      "name": "Success?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [660, 300]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const output = $input.first().json.stdout || '';\n\n// Parse key lines from publish.py output\nconst blogLine = output.match(/Publishing: (.+)/);\nconst tweetLine = output.match(/(\\d+)-tweet thread/);\nconst firstTweetId = output.match(/First tweet ID: (\\d+)/);\nconst logLine = output.match(/Saved to (.+)/);\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    status: 'success',\n    blog_title: blogLine ? blogLine[1] : 'unknown',\n    tweet_count: tweetLine ? tweetLine[1] : '0',\n    first_tweet_id: firstTweetId ? firstTweetId[1] : null,\n    log_file: logLine ? logLine[1] : null,\n    raw_output: output,\n    timestamp: new Date().toISOString()\n  }\n}];"
      },
      "id": "a1b2c3d4-0004-0004-0004-000000000004",
      "name": "Parse Success Output",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [900, 200]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const output = $input.first().json.stdout || '';\nconst stderr = $input.first().json.stderr || '';\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    status: 'error',\n    output: output,\n    stderr: stderr,\n    timestamp: new Date().toISOString()\n  }\n}];"
      },
      "id": "a1b2c3d4-0005-0005-0005-000000000005",
      "name": "Parse Error Output",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [900, 420]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## ✅ Published\n**Blog:** {{ $json.blog_title }}\n**Tweets posted:** {{ $json.tweet_count }}\n**First tweet ID:** {{ $json.first_tweet_id }}\n**Time:** {{ $json.timestamp }}",
        "height": 140,
        "width": 340
      },
      "id": "a1b2c3d4-0006-0006-0006-000000000006",
      "name": "Success Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [1140, 180]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## ❌ Failed\nCheck the raw output:\n```\n{{ $json.output }}\n{{ $json.stderr }}\n```",
        "height": 140,
        "width": 340,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "a1b2c3d4-0007-0007-0007-000000000007",
      "name": "Error Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [1140, 400]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Strategy Blog Publisher\n\n**Schedule:** Every Sunday at 12:00 PM\n\n**What it does:**\n1. Runs `publish.py` in the strategy-blog directory\n2. Publishes the latest blog to prashant-chandel.org\n3. Posts the tweet thread to Twitter/X\n4. Logs the result to `publish-log.json`\n\n**Before first run:**\n- Ensure `strategy-blog/.env` exists with N8N_API_KEY and Twitter credentials\n- Run `pip3 install tweepy requests pyyaml python-dotenv` on this machine\n- Test with `python3 publish.py --dry-run`",
        "height": 240,
        "width": 420,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "a1b2c3d4-0008-0008-0008-000000000008",
      "name": "Setup Notes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [180, 60]
    }
  ],
  "connections": {
    "Every Sunday 12pm": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Run Publisher",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Run Publisher": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Success?",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Success?": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Parse Success Output",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "node": "Parse Error Output",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    }
  },
  "active": false,
  "settings": {
    "executionOrder": "v1",
    "saveManualExecutions": true,
    "callerPolicy": "workflowsFromSameOwner",
    "errorWorkflow": ""
  },
  "versionId": "strategy-blog-v1",
  "meta": {
    "templateCredsSetupCompleted": true,
    "instanceId": "strategy-blog-publisher"
  },
  "tags": ["strategy", "blog", "automation"]
}
